        "completedSourceTexts": [
          {
            "textId": "completed:block:paper-gaokao-2026-ii:grammar-fill:2",
            "paragraphId": "block:paper-gaokao-2026-ii:grammar-fill:2",
            "text": "For the first 15 minutes of my tai chi (太极) class, we remain entirely in one spot to warm up. Angela, a tai chi instructor with twenty-eight years of experience, says that a successful hour of tai chi is an hour with no negative thoughts. “Your mind and body go together. That’s all that matters.”"
          },
          {
            "textId": "completed:block:paper-gaokao-2026-ii:grammar-fill:3",
            "paragraphId": "block:paper-gaokao-2026-ii:grammar-fill:3",
            "text": "Although not a morning person, I begin my lesson with Angela and about twenty others at a Sydney community centre courtyard at 7 am. “Put your feet parallel (平行), and use your dan tian to hold up your body,” she says."
          },
          {
            "textId": "completed:block:paper-gaokao-2026-ii:grammar-fill:4",
            "paragraphId": "block:paper-gaokao-2026-ii:grammar-fill:4",
            "text": "In tai chi, the dan tian is your qi core and qi in Chinese means life force. Now, I am supposed to feel the weight on my legs and sink my dan tian."
          },
          {
            "textId": "completed:block:paper-gaokao-2026-ii:grammar-fill:5",
            "paragraphId": "block:paper-gaokao-2026-ii:grammar-fill:5",
            "text": "We move on to tai chi positions, of which there are forty-two in the style that Angela teaches. Today, we will only be doing the first nine. The movements have descriptive names like “holding the bowl” and “grabbing the bird’s tail.”"
          },
          {
            "textId": "completed:block:paper-gaokao-2026-ii:grammar-fill:6",
            "paragraphId": "block:paper-gaokao-2026-ii:grammar-fill:6",
            "text": "During most of the class, we follow Angela and concentrate on making tiny, isolated (单独) movements. Then, Angela gets us to try the nine movements on our own. I keep my eyes on a woman to my right and try to copy her movements, but unfortunately I soon lose focus."
          },
          {
            "textId": "completed:block:paper-gaokao-2026-ii:grammar-fill:7",
            "paragraphId": "block:paper-gaokao-2026-ii:grammar-fill:7",
            "text": "At the end of the lesson, I feel wide awake, despite it still being early at 8 am. It’s time for my dan tian to meet another life force: coffee."
          }
        ],
